--- a/EN-Enable-radar-tracks(0).md
+++ b/EN-Enable-radar-tracks(0).md
@@ -38 +38 @@ The selected value determines the L1 radar sources and vision matching policy.
-- `0` — Match SCC to vision; use vision when matching fails.
+- `0` — Always use valid SCC range and relative speed; use vision when SCC is absent.
@@ -42,0 +43,2 @@ The selected value determines the L1 radar sources and vision matching policy.
+In versions supporting Bosch MRRevo14F reception, the Bosch path requires startup CAN detection of every `0x601`–`0x612` message, each eight bytes long, on the same receive bus of a non-CAN FD Bosch MRRevo14F candidate (Elantra AD, i30 PD, Kona, Kona Electric, K3 BD/Forte; vehicle-validated only on the Elantra AD). With a positive value, this path passively receives object messages already being transmitted and skips startup radar-activation UDS writes and the request to disable SCC ECU communication.
+
@@ -61,0 +64,2 @@ On a supported radar configuration, change one item at a time and verify detecti
+
+The Bosch passive path does not update `EnableRadarTracksResult`, so a missing or retained value does not indicate current reception success or failure. Restart the vehicle or reboot the device after changing the setting, then check actual message and track reception, CAN validity and radar errors.
@@ -66,0 +71,2 @@ On a supported radar configuration, change one item at a time and verify detecti
+Passive describes radar input reception; it does not put all of carrotpilot into dashcam-only operation or disable steering or longitudinal control. The exception does not apply when Bosch is not detected or the setting is not positive.
+
